==English==

===Etymology===
Originates from the [[1980s]], as slang for the [[stampede]] of people created by a [[police raid]].

Usage occurred May 4th, 1939 in James Joyce's Finnegans Wake meaning to rapidly rush towards and crash against ("... came at this timecoloured place where we live in our paroqial fermament one tide on another, with a bumrush in a hull of a wherry, the twin turbane dhow,").

